1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
And in other news,
there's been a drastic increase

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
in sightings of UMAs,
or Unidentified Mysterious Animals.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
What sets this story apart
from all previous reported phenomena

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
In fact, many of the witnesses
are active members of the police force.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
as first responders were killed.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The images you are seeing

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
are the unidentified creatures
who have been attacking police.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
You can even see the victims on the ground
here near the creature's feet.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
All we know right now

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
but eventually she asked him

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
the one question
that lingers on every viewer's mind.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
[anchorwoman] Those words
would prove to be her last.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[static crackling]

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
but it seems very likely
that they will continue to spread,

15
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
and no effective method
for dealing with them has yet to be found.

16
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
[opening theme music playing]

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

18
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

19
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
[singer singing in English]

20
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
we can infer that they most likely
came from the Balsa Islands.

21
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
There sure are
a lot of weird nations in that area.

22
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Both the NGL
and the Republic of East Gorteau

23
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
are nations that choose to be
completely isolationist.

24
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
They're a whole lot
like this place, in fact.

25
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[Bonolenov] I suppose that would make it
easier for the Ants to invade.

26
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
[birds squawking]

27
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Wow. It's been a while, huh?

28
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
[Phinks] Hasn't changed a bit.

29
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
-[footsteps approaching]
-Huh?

30
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
we're seeing over 300 dead.

31
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Bombs have no effect,
so we can't fight back against them.

32
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
[man] A few days ago,
he was an ordinary human.

33
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
So the Ants did this?

34
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
He's dead as a doornail, if you ask me.

35
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
The Assembly's debate right now
is if they should be declared dead

36
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,000
based on whether or not there's a way
to restore them to their original forms.

37
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Okay, let me get this straight.
They can't avenge them,

38
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
They always lose sight
of what's important,

39
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
so we're gonna do things our way.

40
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
If anyone interferes,
we'll take them down,

41
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
as simple as that.

42
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,000
[Phinks] Before the day's over,
we'll exterminate this so-called queen.

43
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
My mother's greatest flaw

44
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
was that she could only produce soldiers
by laying eggs,

45
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
an archaic
and highly inefficient practice.

46
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Her only success…

47
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
was giving birth to me.

48
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Stop. Kill me! Just kill me!

49
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[growls]

50
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[Shalnark] Let's try the front door.

51
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Phinks] Sounds good to me.

52
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Nobody's here.

53
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
So are they inviting us all inside
or what?

54
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
I'll go this way, I suppose.

55
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
And I'll go this way.

56
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
You probably have abilities you don't want
to reveal to us either, right?

57
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[Kalluto] Understood.

58
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
[all] Start!

59
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
They've all scattered.

60
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Judging by their footsteps,

61
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
I can sense that
these particular intruders are special,

62
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
[Zazan] Are they strong?

63
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[Pike] They are.

64
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[Zazan] Then go and get them.

65
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I can't. If I did, then no one would
be here to protect you, Your Majesty.

66
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Be careful, Pike. I'm counting on you.

67
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
[gasps] I shall.

68
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Be right back!

69
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
[Zazan] Well, now then…

70
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[servant] Off to join the fray?

71
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
[Zazan] My mother's greatest misfortune

72
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:06,000
was that she never experienced
the joy of combat.

73
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[Chimera Ant] You're no fun.

74
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Just let me hold you,

75
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[narrator] Bonolenov is descended
from the Gyudondond people,

76
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:05,000
a small tribe chased into obliteration
by industrialization of their land.

77
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
When Gyudondond males
reach the age of three,

78
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,000
needles are used
to puncture holes in their bodies.

79
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
By performing different movements,

80
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
They are known as the Bap,
"dancing warriors."

81
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
Prologue!

82
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
that you will never defeat me.

83
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[Chimera Ant] Hold on.

84
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
[Bonolenov] Don't bother
recanting those words.

85
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
They are nothing more
than the ramblings of a beast.

86
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
They cannot affect me.

87
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[Shalnark] In a one-on-one fight,
my opponent's strength doesn't matter.

88
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
If I can stab them with this, I'll win.

89
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
But can I pierce that?

90
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[grunts]

91
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Those are pretty sharp.

92
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
The probability
of succeeding unscathed is 20%.

93
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
What the…

94
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Why didn't it work?

95
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I could have sworn I put the antenna in.

96
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
[Chimera Ant] You must be a Manipulator.

97
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
That must be the main condition
for activating your power.

98
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
You let your guard down
when you thought it had worked.

99
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
[Shalnark] Wow. This thing's name is Pell?

100
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
-You're a Manipulator, too?
-Huh?

101
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:58,000
My ability didn't activate
even though the conditions were met.

102
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
I'm very impressed that you could tell.

103
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
It's first come, first served
for Manipulators here.

104
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,000
And now all that remains for me
is to take you directly to the Queen,

105
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
and my job will be complete.

106
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[Shalnark grunting]

107
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
I'm gonna give you just one more attack
before I finish you off.

108
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
You know some pretty big words
for a stupid Ant.

109
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Fine. I'll take you up on that offer.
I choose a punch.

110
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[gasps]

111
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
That one makes 11. Almost there.

112
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen!

113
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Wait! Please, no!

114
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
KARMIC LOOP

115
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[Phinks] Every time I wind my arm,
my punch gets stronger.

116
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Ripper Cyclotron!

117
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Oh, wow. Guess half of that
would have been enough by the looks of it.

118
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
I never know
exactly how much power to use.

119
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,000
Now, then, which way to go?

120
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Right or left?

121
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
I'll just flip a coin.

122
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Okay, so what's going to happen to me now?

123
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
[Chimera Ant] You'll become a slave.

124
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
You'll work for the Queen
until the day you die.

125
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Not much different
from your current life, really.

126
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[laughs] There's some truth to that.

127
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
It seems the only real difference
would be in whom I'm working for.

128
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
But if my choices are
die or listen to you,

129
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
[gasps] He just stabbed himself!

130
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[automated female voice] Autopilot on.

131
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
[Chimera Ant gasps]

132
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
That's so much aura!

133
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Terminate target.

134
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Hurry up, Pell! Take his leg!
Remove the antenna!

135
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
I bet I'll be too sore to move a muscle
for at least a couple of days.

136
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
That's why I hate using this mode.

137
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
[Blinky babbles]

138
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Ooh! Pretty powerful
for a little girl, aren't you?

139
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
I wonder where she was hiding that vacuum.

140
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
[Shizuku] The thread's strong.

141
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
If I get caught,
I won't be able to escape.

142
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
[Feitan] Not a funny joke.

143
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
What? A joke?

144
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
[over transmission] Brats like you
deserve to be punished severely.

145
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
[Bonolenov] They are nothing more
than the ramblings of a beast.

146
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
[Phinks] Fine.
I'll take you up on that offer.

147
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[Shalnark] You know what? When I fight,
I always carry two antennae with me.

148
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
I wonder how I intercept.

149
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[Chimera Ant] What's this? A child?

150
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
All right, little girl. Come over here.

151
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
[sighs]

152
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

153
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[laughs] Okay. What's that?

154
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Surrounding me with more paper?

155
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[gasps]

156
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
You like hiding things on you, little boy?

157
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[Feitan] As do you.

158
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
[choking]

159
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
[whistling continues]

160
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:29,000
What's the matter?
Weren't you attacking me?

161
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,000
I just assumed that you wanted
to stop my performance.

162
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
[screams]

163
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
[laughs] You'll pay for this!

164
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
I'll get Pike
to tangle this guy up in his thread

165
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
so he can't make a sound.

166
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Well, you certainly do escape quickly,

167
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
but not nearly as fast
as the speed of sound.

168
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[rumbling]

169
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
[Bonolenov] Battle Cantabile…

170
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Squashed to death. What a tragedy.

171
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[narrator] The Phantom Troupe
fight valiantly

172
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:05,000
to protect Meteor City, their home,
from the Chimera Ants.

173
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
[closing theme music playing]

174
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

175
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[upbeat music playing]

176
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Killua] Nog, erus.

177
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,000
[Gon] Hey, what did we just say?

178
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,000
[Killua] Hint: it was backwards.
